From 17c5c5542e72d41bbd956398b644fc878a704fe9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 20:01:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 135/254] feat(pypto-x): ingest the opt-in tied lm_head dual
 packing (W8C 556 open)

Allow one checkpoint tensor to back two logical parameters when it is the
frozen contract 0002 section 3.4 pair (BF16 embedding + int8 lm_head packing)
while every other duplicate claim, missing tensor, dangling scale or shape
mismatch stays fail-closed.  The checkpoint-aware layout now models
quant_weight/quant_scale regions and only admits an overlap when both regions
reference the identical registered source range.  Physical checkpoint bytes are
deduplicated with an explicit shared-source overcount so the byte
conservation identity holds; the streaming weight quantizer keeps the tied
lm_head (248320x1024) fp64 working set bounded and stays bit-exact with the
C1 golden.  BF16 layout JSON/digest is byte-identical.
